  "notes": "Portal source: app/modules/tools_tab/tools/chla_tool.R, calculate observer lines 274-496. The observer loops replicates A-E (line 279) and computes BOTH the acid and the no-acid variant for every replicate unconditionally (lines 308-351): there is no method switch, so v1's method enum is gone and both variants appear together whenever their curve is selected. Per replicate the portal also derives lab_chla_vol_filtrated_rep_X = calcMinus(tot_vol, vol_after) (296-306), afdm_g_filter_rep_X = calcMinus(lab_chla_wgt_1_rep_X, lab_chla_wgt_2_rep_X) (353-363), the two calcChlaPerM2 conversions (380-401) and calcBenthicAFDM (403-413); the avg/sd loop (444-492) writes ten summary columns, four of them the chla SDs v1 dropped. Column spellings are the portal's, including the Chla_{variant}_{avg|sd}_ugm2 vs Chla_{variant}_ugL_{avg|sd} asymmetry the naming branch at 455-462 produces. The two standard curves are the portal's two selectInputs (40-61), so they are manifest curve slots (chla_acid, chla_noacid), not request slope/intercept numbers. KEEP OLD is NOT emulated: the portal falls back to the stored cell via pull(row(), col) (e.g. 326-330), which a stateless tool has no access to, so a KEEP OLD becomes NA and the key is omitted, matching the tools tab dropping NAs. Expected values are derived from the portal formulas (calcChlaAcid = (f1-f2)*a+b, calcChlaNoAcid = f1*a+b, calcChlaPerM2 = convertToUnitPerM2(ugL*0.005, sizes, vol_filtrated, tot_vol), calcBenthicAFDM = convertToUnitPerM2(afdm_g, ...), mean/sd over the non-NA replicates with R's n-1 sd) and confirmed against the live runner. Non-finite values are portal values, not sentinels: the portal's ifelse(x != 'KEEP OLD', x, ...) compares a numeric against a string, so an Inf (reachable when lab_chla_vol_after == lab_chla_tot_vol makes vol_filtrated 0 and convertToUnitPerM2 divides by it) tests TRUE and is stored, then propagates into calcChlaPerM2/calcBenthicAFDM and into calcMean/calcSd. The wrapper therefore converts only the 'KEEP OLD' string to NA and applies no plausibility filter: an Inf or NaN is emitted as the portal would display it, and reaches the caller as an absent key only because JSON cannot encode either (both serialise to null under na=null and the API drops nulls). zero_volume_filtrated_makes_per_m2_infinite pins this: replicate A's per-m2 keys are Inf, the acid/no-acid per-m2 family mean is therefore Inf and its sd NaN, so all of them are absent from the response rather than the aggregate falling back to replicate B's finite value. benthic_AFDM_avg_gm2 and its sd are absent for the same reason.",
